-- Catalog seeds for the multi-provider inference router (docs/architecture/
-- multi-provider-inference-implementation.md) and ADR-explicit-device-local-models.md.
--
-- Three on-device models (execution target "browser-local", provider "local"): each one names an
-- entry in the pinned @mlc-ai/web-llm package's own prebuilt model list, and the web client only
-- ever loads such entries from the approved https://huggingface.co/mlc-ai/ origin. They cost
-- nothing to run (pricing 0) and never send conversation text to a cloud model.
--
-- One Grogoni Cloud entry (Qwen3-4B on Grogoni's own llama.cpp server) seeded *disabled*: it only works
-- after an operator sets GROGONI_LLAMA_BASE_URL and flips `available` / `inference.enabled` through
-- PUT /v1/platform/model-catalog/:id.
--
-- Commercial vendor models (OpenAI, Anthropic, Z.ai) are deliberately not seeded: their model ids
-- and prices change and must be verified by the operator registering them.
--
-- `on conflict do nothing`: an operator's existing row with the same id is never overwritten.
